  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer (config_006, acc=0.653) is the clear best configuration, far exceeding image-only models (≤0.227). The multiprofile setting and scvi_n200 encoder are strongly validated. Uncertainty: it is unknown whether adding the image modality (very weak alone) provides complementary signal to the already-strong RNA representation, or whether it introduces noise. This experiment (config_032: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is the direct multimodal extension of config_006, changing only the addition of image + concat fusion. This isolates the effect of the image modality against the best known RNA baseline. It is the most informative next step because it answers the central question—does multimodal fusion improve upon the strong RNA-only result—before committing budget to further multimodal variants (weighted fusion, ViT, scgpt). If it fails to beat 0.653, it saves many downstream multimodal experiments; if it succeeds, it justifies exploring fusion type and image encoder."
}

